<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander Bustamante</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1884">1884</a>–<a href="/years/1977">1977</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander Bustamante was a Jamaican labour leader and politician who rose to prominence in the labour unrest of 1938. He founded the Bustamante Industrial Trade Union and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica-labour-party">Jamaica Labour Party</a>, and won the first election under universal suffrage in 1944. He campaigned against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-indies">West Indies</a> Federation and became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a>'s first prime minister at independence in 1962, serving until 1967.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-bustamante.jpg" alt="Alexander Bustamante" width="170" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Robert Knudsen. White House Photographs. John F. Kennedy Presidential Library and Museum, Boston · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prime_Minister_of_Jamaica,_Sir_Alexander_Bustamante_(04)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
